<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">3 January in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">12 events that happened on 3 January, from 250 to 2004.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/roman-empire.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">250 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,776 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Emperor Decius orders all Romans to sacrifice to the gods</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Decius required every inhabitant of the empire to sacrifice before officials and obtain a certificate proving it. Christians who refused faced death, in the first empire-wide persecution of the Church.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1521">1521 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">505 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pope Leo X excommunicates Martin Luther</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The bull Decet Romanum Pontificem formally cut <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/martin-luther">Martin Luther</a> off from the Catholic Church after he refused to recant. The break hardened the divide that became the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Protestant Reformation</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Protestant Reformation</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1777">1777 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">249 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Washington defeats the British at the Battle of Princeton</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After a night march from Trenton, Washington's army routed a British force at Princeton, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-jersey">New Jersey</a>. Coming days after Trenton, the victory revived the American cause and pushed the British out of most of New Jersey.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1833">1833 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">193 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Britain reasserts control over the Falkland Islands</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">HMS Clio under Captain James Onslow arrived at the Falklands and required the small Argentine garrison at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/port-louis">Port Louis</a> to leave. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argentina">Argentina</a> has disputed British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a> over the islands ever since.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argentina">Argentina</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1848">1848 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">178 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Joseph Jenkins Roberts becomes Liberia's first president</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joseph-jenkins-roberts">Joseph Jenkins Roberts</a>, born free in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a>, was inaugurated as president of the newly independent Republic of Liberia. Liberia became the first independent republic in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1868">1868 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">158 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Meiji Restoration returns power to Japan's emperor</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Forces from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/satsuma-domain">Satsuma</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/choshu-domain">Choshu</a> seized the imperial palace in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyoto">Kyoto</a> and an imperial decree abolished the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-shogunate">Tokugawa shogunate</a>. The young <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-meiji">Emperor Meiji</a>'s government launched <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>'s rapid modernisation.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/tokugawa-shogunate">Tokugawa Shogunate</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meiji-restoration">Meiji Restoration</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-meiji">Emperor Meiji</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyoto">Kyoto</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1870">1870 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">156 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Construction of the Brooklyn Bridge begins</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Work started on John Roebling's suspension bridge across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a>'s East River. Completed in 1883 under his son Washington and daughter-in-law Emily, it was then the longest suspension bridge in the world.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1925">1925 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">101 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mussolini's speech to parliament opens his dictatorship</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In a speech to the Italian Chamber of Deputies, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benito-mussolini">Mussolini</a> declared he alone took responsibility for all that had happened, including the murder of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giacomo-matteotti">Giacomo Matteotti</a>. The speech launched his open dictatorship.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1947">1947 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">79 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">US Congress proceedings are televised for the first time</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The opening session of the 80th Congress was broadcast on television, a first for the American legislature. Regular television coverage of both chambers followed only decades later.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1959">1959 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">67 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Alaska becomes the 49th US state</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dwight-d-eisenhower">Eisenhower</a> signed the proclamation admitting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alaska">Alaska</a> to the Union. Purchased from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> in 1867, it became the largest state by area, more than twice the size of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/texas">Texas</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alaska">Alaska</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1993">1993 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">33 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Bush and Yeltsin sign the START II arms treaty</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a>, George H. W. Bush and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boris-yeltsin">Boris Yeltsin</a> agreed to cut their strategic nuclear arsenals by about two-thirds and ban multiple-warhead land-based missiles. The treaty never fully entered into force.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/2004">2004 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">22 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">NASA's Spirit rover lands in Mars's Gusev Crater</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Cushioned by airbags, Spirit bounced to a halt on Mars on the evening of 3 January, US time. Planned to last 90 days, it explored for over six years and found evidence of past water.</p></div></li></ol>
